# Suppresses everything the target leaks, to prove that a suppression file can
# turn a failing run into a passing one -- and that the suppressed leaks are
# still counted in summary.suppressedByRules rather than vanishing.
#
# Note how broad this is. Matching the target's own module means "anything whose
# stack passes through this binary", which is every allocation the program made,
# including the ones libc made on its behalf. That is the intended reach of a
# `stack:` rule and the reason to prefer `function:` when you can name the site.
stack:*multiple_leaks*
